[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define a pure, ordered save-migration runner that accepts an untrusted saved
[stderr] +candidate, declares supported predecessor versions, and promotes only a fully
[stderr] +validated result. Failed or unsupported candidates retain their original bytes
[stderr] +and quarantine disposition; this contract does not select storage or repair
[stderr] +player data destructively.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0005 owns the versioned content and provenance schema boundary. R0006 owns
[stderr] +the local save, validation, current-pointer, known-good retention, and
[stderr] +quarantine protocol. Both are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0003 /
[stderr] +DEC-0003: a human decision is required for the supported migration window,
[stderr] +storage API, quota, and recovery policy before implementation relies on them.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/` migration registry and runner.
[stderr] +- `tests/core/save/fixtures/` predecessor, unsupported-version, and failed
[stderr] +  candidate fixtures.
[stderr] +- Migration registry data and the migration-runner API.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The runner owns only pure candidate transformations and their validation
[stderr] +boundary. R0006 retains persistence, pointer promotion, and quarantine record
[stderr] +ownership; adapters retain any future approved storage mechanism.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Represent every migration as an ordered pure transformation from one declared
[stderr] +schema version to its immediate successor. The runner must not read storage,
[stderr] +write storage, access a clock, mutate its input, or choose a current save. It
[stderr] +returns either one validated candidate with its resulting version or a typed
[stderr] +failure that leaves the supplied bytes and source version available to R0006's
[stderr] +quarantine path.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Before promotion, validate the complete transformed candidate using the save
[stderr] +schema, checksum/integrity process, and applicable invariants. Execute each
[stderr] +predecessor step once in ascending order; reject cycles, duplicate version
[stderr] +steps, gaps, unknown versions, and a result that cannot validate. Do not retry
[stderr] +by guessing, drop unknown fields silently, fabricate content, or repair data
[stderr] +in place. Only R0006's existing recovery protocol may retain or quarantine the
[stderr] +original candidate and promote a validated replacement.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Responsive web and installed PWA consume the same shared pure migration API.
[stderr] +Their eventual approved local-storage adapters may pass bytes into the runner,
[stderr] +but neither target gets a separate migration sequence. PWA cache and update
[stderr] +records never enter migration input and cannot be promoted as save data.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not choose a storage driver, support window, retention policy, or recovery
[stderr] +policy; do not modify adapters, cache lifecycle, content packages, or current
[stderr] +pointers. Do not add export/import, cloud sync, accounts, remote services,
[stderr] +network transport, automatic destructive repair, UI, gameplay, product assets,
[stderr] +or audio.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The migration runner and synthetic
[stderr] +predecessor fixtures need no product asset. Do not create or reserve visual,
[stderr] +source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other
[stderr] +incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Run deterministic fixtures for every declared predecessor and prove each
[stderr] +  takes its ordered path exactly once to a validated candidate.
[stderr] +- Prove unsupported versions, duplicate/gapped/cyclic registry definitions,
[stderr] +  thrown transformations, checksum failures, and invariant failures leave the
[stderr] +  original bytes intact and route to the typed failure/quarantine boundary.
[stderr] +- Prove the runner has no storage, network, clock, cache, pointer-promotion,
[stderr] +  or mutation dependency; web and PWA adapter fixtures use the same API.
[stderr] +- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its
