[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define a bounded, privacy-safe local diagnostic contract for future recovery
[stderr] +support: an explicitly consented, redacted local record, clear/delete controls,
[stderr] +and a recorder interface with no transport. It must help diagnose a recovery
[stderr] +condition without collecting save bytes, dialogue, identity, secrets, or a
[stderr] +remote analytics payload.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic
[stderr] +fixtures, and R0006 provides local save/recovery and quarantine boundaries.
[stderr] +Retain GATE-0005 / DEC-0005: a human decision is required before any transport,
[stderr] +retention, hosting, support, or data-handling claim. The gate blocks those
[stderr] +implementation choices, not authoring this local boundary.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/platform/web/diagnostics/` local diagnostic adapter boundary.
[stderr] +- `src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*` consent, record, redaction, and
[stderr] +  clear-control interface.
[stderr] +- `tests/platform/diagnostics.*` deterministic consent, redaction, and local
[stderr] +  deletion fixtures.
[stderr] +- `docs/privacy-and-recovery.md` diagnostic boundary documentation.
[stderr] +- Redacted local diagnostic record and consent-state data schemas.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The shared core does not own diagnostic storage or transport. R0006 owns save
[stderr] +data and recovery; this task may reference only stable non-content failure
[stderr] +categories needed for a local recovery record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Default diagnostics to absent. The recorder creates a record only after an
[stderr] +explicit, revocable local consent state is present; a missing, declined, or
[stderr] +withdrawn consent state must create no record. Define a small allow-list such
[stderr] +as schema-safe failure category, local timestamp abstraction, app/build
[stderr] +identifier placeholder, and recovery action outcome only where the relevant
[stderr] +human decisions permit a value. Redact or reject all unrecognised fields.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Never capture save snapshots or bytes, checksums, slot names, preferences,
[stderr] +dialogue, authored content, free text, input sequences, account data, device
[stderr] +identifiers, IP/network data, cookies, tokens, credentials, stack payloads
[stderr] +that can expose content, or secrets. Provide a clear-local-record operation
[stderr] +that removes only diagnostics after explicit confirmation and visibly reports
[stderr] +the local result. The record must not influence save recovery or block play.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Enforce a no-network boundary: no provider, endpoint, request client, beacon,
[stderr] +upload queue, analytics SDK, background sync, remote retention, or export path
[stderr] +is permitted. A future transport proposal is separate work and remains halted
[stderr] +at GATE-0005 / DEC-0005.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and installed PWA share the same consent, redaction, clear, and no-network
[stderr] +contract. PWA installation, cache, or offline update state does not grant a
[stderr] +diagnostic upload or a separate retention policy. Any target-local storage
[stderr] +mechanism remains unselected until the retained gate is resolved.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not integrate analytics, crash reporting, telemetry providers, transport,
[stderr] +hosting, remote support, retention schedules, export, identifiers, secrets,
[stderr] +accounts, sync, network services, UI screens, save-content inspection,
[stderr] +product assets, or audio. Do not claim legal, compliance, or support approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. Local redacted records, consent state, and
[stderr] +deterministic fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve
[stderr] +visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or
[stderr] +other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Run deterministic fixtures proving no record is created without consent and
[stderr] +  that withdrawal prevents subsequent recording.
[stderr] +- Test allow-list redaction against save bytes, dialogue/content, slot data,
[stderr] +  identifiers, credentials, tokens, request/endpoint fields, stack payloads,
[stderr] +  and unknown properties; all must be omitted or rejected.
[stderr] +- Test explicit local deletion removes only diagnostic records and leaves the
[stderr] +  save/recovery boundary unchanged.
[stderr] +- Run a static dependency scan proving no network, transport, provider,
[stderr] +  analytics, upload, or background-sync import/configuration exists.
[stderr] +- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its
[stderr] +  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the
[stderr] +  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0009 and never renumber or replace it.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain consent-state and absent-record fixture results, redaction/rejection
[stderr] +assertions, local-clear results, no-network scan output, the retained
[stderr] +GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 record, and the successful loader and manifest-comparison
[stderr] +record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Diagnostics are absent without consent, contain only allow-listed redacted
[stderr] +  local fields, and can be explicitly deleted without affecting save data.
[stderr] +- No diagnostic payload includes save or dialogue data, identity, secrets, or
[stderr] +  network/transport fields; no remote diagnostics path is introduced.
[stderr] +- Transport, retention, hosting, and support decisions remain blocked by
[stderr] +  GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 for both web and PWA paths.
