[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define the original-content provenance control that makes each later authored
[stderr] +content package auditable before it enters a build. The control supplies a
[stderr] +provenance-record format, source-asset manifest input, validator contract, and
[stderr] +human creative-review disposition without creating art, audio, story, or legal
[stderr] +approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0005 provides the versioned content package, asset/provenance-manifest schema,
[stderr] +and validator boundary. It is the implementation dependency. Human creative
[stderr] +review is mandatory for every authored package; legal or licensing review,
[stderr] +where applicable, remains under GATE-0007 and cannot be inferred or automated.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `assets/source-manifest.*` provenance input format for later authored
[stderr] +  content/assets.
[stderr] +- `docs/original-content-review.md` review checklist and recorded disposition.
[stderr] +- `tests/content/provenance.*` missing-field and review-state fixtures.
[stderr] +- Provenance manifest, review disposition data, and provenance-validator input
[stderr] +  contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0005 retains content-schema and registry ownership. This task owns only the
[stderr] +evidence required to admit later authored material; it does not own assets,
[stderr] +licences, gameplay content, or release packaging.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Require a stable content-package reference and a complete provenance record
[stderr] +for every later authored content, visual, audio, localisation, map, dialogue,
[stderr] +or other expressive entry. The record must identify the entry, its authoring
[stderr] +source/type, original-work assertion, any declared permitted source or licence
[stderr] +reference when applicable, review status, reviewer identity/role placeholder,
[stderr] +review date placeholder, and a human creative-review disposition. Keep the
[stderr] +functional reference boundary explicit: a compact party-based turn-adventure
[stderr] +scope may inform function only; names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts,
[stderr] +UI flows, interaction choreography, and other expression must be original.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The validator rejects a missing record, missing required fields, unmatched
[stderr] +content reference, invalid disposition, or an entry not marked ready after
[stderr] +human creative review. It must not infer originality from an asset filename,
[stderr] +automatically clear legal rights, or create substitute content. A reviewer may
[stderr] +record a hold or reject disposition; only the human reviewer can record the
[stderr] +creative-review outcome. Where a declared source signals licensing or legal
[stderr] +review, retain GATE-0007 rather than allowing a technical validator to approve
[stderr] +it.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
