---
task_id: B0005
sequence: 6
title: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts
browser_impact: not_applicable
playwright_spec:
---

## Objective

After B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and
`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named
human gates.

## Context packet

Read the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,
`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,
`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,
`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and
`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.

## Output list

- `../runbooks/R0007.md` — IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.
- `../runbooks/R0009.md` — IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.
- `../runbooks/R0011.md` — IMP-0011; dependency R0005.

## Required authoring content

Use standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:
B0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and
blank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,
requirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform
differences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset
assessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.

## Validation procedure

Stop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their
metadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify
required sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.

## Checkpoint and update procedure

Checkpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted
outputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.

## Stop condition

Stop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.

## Acceptance criteria

- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.
- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.
- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.
- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.
