P-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n29-  },\n30:  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n31-}\n---\ntask_id: R0008\nsequence: 8\ntitle: Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\ndependencies: R0002,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0013,REQ-0014,REQ-0015,NFR-0012\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0008\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; a negative scope boundary.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDocument and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and\nresume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization\nrole, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local\ncampaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain\nGATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,\nprivacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `docs/security-boundary.md`.\n- `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.\n- The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity\n  contract.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nState that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account\nor authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has\nno remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud\nbackup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque\nlocal reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote\nprofile fields.\n\nAdd negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation\nmodules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or\nserver clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,\npurchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if\never approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nResponsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same\nconnected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage\ndo not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target\nobtains a distinct connected implementation path.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not implement sign-in, OAuth, accounts, profiles, tokens, roles,\nauthorization, synchronization, server APIs, analytics transport, multiplayer,\nmoderation, reporting, purchases, entitlements, cloud saves, remote\ndiagnostics, or security claims about a device owner. Do not create product\nassets, audio, or connected-service configuration.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is documentation and negative test\ncoverage for an architectural exclusion. Do not create or reserve incidental\nvisual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\nother product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run a static scan across P0 foundation modules for prohibited identity,\n  token, privilege, entitlement, and network/server-client fields or imports.\n- Run negative fixtures that attempt prohibited connected-scope configuration\n  and prove the contract rejects or does not expose it.\n- Verify start, local save, and local resume fixtures require only a local slot\n  reference and no remote request or account data.\n- Review `docs/security-boundary.md` against the exclusion list and record\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 as retained for any future connected proposal.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain static-scan and negative-fixture results, local start/save/resume test\noutput showing no remote request, the security-boundary review, and the future\nconnected-service approval checklist with its retained gate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- P0 start, save, and resume expose no identity, token, role, entitlement,\n  remote-profile, or network-client field or dependency.\n- Negative tests prevent connected-service scope from entering P0 foundation\n  modules for both web and PWA delivery paths.\n- Any future connected work remains outside campaign truth and blocked by\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 rather than implicitly approved.\n---\ntask_id: R0006\nsequence: 6\ntitle: Specify local save and recovery protocol\ndependencies: R0002,R0003,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003,NFR-0005\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0006\nauthoring_batch: B0004\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; this is a local data and recovery protocol.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nSpecify the bounded, local save and recovery protocol for immutable revisions,\nchecksums, validated current pointers, known-good retention, quarantine,\nseparate preferences, explicit deletion, and save-safe boundaries. This is a\nprotocol and fixture contract, not approval to select a browser-storage API or\npromise a quota, retention period, or migration-support window.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 provides the core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic clock and\npersistence fixtures, and R0004 supplies the immutable versioned campaign\nsnapshot and command/revision contracts. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: storage\nAPI, quota, support window, and recovery policy require human approval before\nimplementation selects or relies on them. The gate blocks implementation\nchoices, not this contract's authoring.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/` protocol contracts.\n- `src/platform/web/persistence/` adapter boundary.\n- `tests/{core,platform}/save*` fault and recovery fixtures.\n- `docs/save-and-recovery.md`.\n- Snapshot/preference/quarantine schemas and snapshot-repository/recovery API.\n\nThe shared layer owns snapshot shape, validation, compatibility, and recovery\nsemantics. The web adapter owns only the eventual approved local-storage\nmechanism. PWA cache/install lifecycle, content registry, remote sync,\nidentity, diagnostics transport, and campaign transitions are not owned here.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nUse a write-ahead replacement protocol: serialize a complete immutable\nsnapshot, validate checksum/schema/invariants, write a new revision candidate,\nverify read-back, atomically mark a validated current pointer (or emulate it\nwith immutable records), and retain the prior known-good snapshot. Never clear\nor overwrite the prior confirmed save until the new pointer is valid. Separate\npreferences from campaign snapshots and never treat a cache record as a save.\n\nValidate bounded, untrusted persisted bytes before parsing or use. A malformed,\nchecksum-invalid, incompatible, or migration-failed candidate is preserved with\nits metadata in quarantine; it never replaces a valid save. Recovery offers\nthe last valid checkpoint or a clear new-game/fallback route. Loading restores\nonly safe scene boundaries. A failed quota, permission, or unavailable-storage\nattempt leaves the session playable, says persistence did not succeed, and\noffers non-blocking retry guidance.\n\nPersist only at explicit safe boundaries: no unresolved combat turn or partial\ncommand can become current. A stale writer must fail rather than replace the\nlatest revision. Deletion requires an explicit confirmation naming the selected\nslot and its available progress/time; initial focus is Cancel, repeated/stale\ninput cannot activate Delete, and only that local slot and its recovery\nmetadata are removed.\n\nMigration transformations remain ordered pure candidate transformations and\nare not implemented or approved here beyond their compatibility boundary; R0007\nowns the migration runner. No cloud, account, sync, cross-device merge, cache\neviction, or export/import promise is introduced.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and installed PWA share the same local snapshot, preference, validation,\nquarantine, and recovery contract. The web adapter eventually binds an approved\nsame-origin storage mechanism; the PWA inherits it and must keep its\nservice-worker cache separate. A cache refresh or update failure neither\ndeletes, refreshes, nor synchronises save data, and no implementation may\nclaim persistence after an unconfirmed write.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not choose a storage API, quota, eviction guarantee, support window,\nretention policy, or migration set before GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 approval. Do not\nimplement cloud sync, accounts, remote deletion, cross-device conflict\nresolution, PWA cache lifecycle, release update flow, diagnostics transport,\ncontent validation, gameplay, UI screens, product assets, or audio.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: local snapshots, protocol interfaces, and\nfault fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental\nvisual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other\nproduct asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run deterministic fault fixtures for interrupted write, failed read-back,\n  checksum failure, malformed/oversized bytes, unsupported version, storage\n  quota/permission/unavailable failures, stale writer, quarantine, retry, and\n  selected-slot deletion confirmation.\n- Prove each failure preserves the last valid snapshot, does not report a save\n  as successful, keeps the session usable where possible, and exposes the\n  required retry/title/fallback/new-game recovery choice.\n- Prove a current-pointer promotion occurs only after candidate validation and\n  read-back; prove preferences and PWA cache fixtures cannot be read as or\n  overwrite a campaign snapshot.\n- Prove a pending command or unresolved combat turn cannot be committed and a\n  stale/repeated delete action cannot remove an unselected slot.\n- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0006, dependencies\n  match the manifest, owned paths do not overlap R0005's content boundary, and\n  every required section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain deterministic fault-fixture output, pre/post candidate and pointer\nrecords, quarantine and recovery-path assertions, preference/save/cache\nseparation evidence, deletion-confirmation assertions, the retained\nGATE-0003 / DEC-0003 record, and the pre-checkpoint loader, provenance,\ndependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Interrupted, invalid, incompatible, or failed save candidates cannot replace\n  a validated current snapshot; the prior known-good snapshot is retained or\n  malformed bytes are quarantined.\n- Save snapshots, preferences, and PWA cache records remain separate, and\n  local recovery presents clear retry, title, fallback, or new-game choices\n  without claiming an unconfirmed save succeeded.\n- Storage selection, quota, support window, migration policy, and recovery\n  policy remain blocked by GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no remote, cache, or asset\n  work is introduced.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files runbooks projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 | rg '(TEMPLATE|F014|runbook.*(load|valid)|author)' | sed -n '1,160p'; rg -n 'runbook loader|manifest comparison|provenance|required sections|R0007' scripts supervisor runbooks projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 -g '*.py' -g '*.sh' -g '*.md' | sed -n '1,220p'\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nrunbooks/F014.md\nrunbooks/TEMPLATE.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0002.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0006.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/C0001.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0001.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0004.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md:47:with provenance and human creative review.\nrunbooks/F014.md:44:Every generated R-series runbook must retain machine-readable provenance to the\nrunbooks/F014.md:99:ACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For\nrunbooks/F014.md:137:  and `factory_stages` provenance metadata.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md:29:Use exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch: B0003`, standard\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md:40:provenance, dependencies, and ownership with the manifest; and verify every\nrunbooks/F015.md:21: 