horing system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:13:| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:16:The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:28:| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:32:| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:39:Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:41:At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:69:def test_r_series_runbook_must_declare_provenance(tmp_path):\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:72:        \"---\\ntask_id: R0001\\nsequence: 1\\ntitle: Missing provenance\\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\\nplaywright_spec:\\nasset_impact: not_applicable\\nasset_ids:\\n---\\n\"\nsupervisor/tests/test_runbooks.py:77:    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"must declare provenance metadata\"):\nsupervisor/tests/test_art_pipeline.py:34:def test_art_director_records_original_art_provenance(tmp_path):\nsupervisor/tests/test_art_pipeline.py:39:    assert manifest[\"provenance\"][\"original_only\"] is True\nsupervisor/scripts/asset_qa_worker.py:68:    # or expensively on a local machine.  Technical/provenance QA is mandatory;\nsupervisor/scripts/asset_qa_worker.py:84:            elif not manifest.get(\"provenance\", {}).get(\"original_only\"):\nsupervisor/scripts/asset_qa_worker.py:85:                errors.append(f\"{asset_id}: original-art provenance not recorded\")\nsupervisor/scripts/audio_qa_worker.py:34:            elif not manifest.get(\"provenance\", {}).get(\"original_only\"):\nsupervisor/scripts/audio_qa_worker.py:35:                errors.append(f\"{audio_id}: original-audio provenance is not recorded\")\nsupervisor/tests/test_audio_pipeline.py:63:    assert manifest[\"provenance\"][\"original_only\"] is True\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md; sed -n '1,180p' runbooks/TEMPLATE.md; sed -n '1,190p' runbooks/F014.md; sed -n '1,220p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n---\ntask_id: B0005\nsequence: 6\ntitle: Author migration diagnostics and provenance contracts\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nAfter B0004, create only `../runbooks/R0007.md`, `../runbooks/R0009.md`, and\n`../runbooks/R0011.md` for IMP-0007, IMP-0009, and IMP-0011. Retain all named\nhuman gates.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead the B0005/R0007/R0009/R0011 manifest records and catalogue records,\n`../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics`,\n`03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security`,\n`01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary`, and\n`04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary`.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0007.md` \u2014 IMP-0007; dependencies R0005,R0006.\n- `../runbooks/R0009.md` \u2014 IMP-0009; dependencies R0002,R0003,R0006.\n- `../runbooks/R0011.md` \u2014 IMP-0011; dependency R0005.\n\n## Required authoring content\n\nUse standard front matter and exact manifest provenance with `authoring_batch:\nB0005`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, `asset_impact: not_applicable`, and\nblank `asset_ids`. Each small R task must provide objective, dependencies,\nrequirements, files/data/interfaces, required behaviour, non-goals, platform\ndifferences, verification/evidence, observable criteria, and an `## Asset\nassessment` prohibiting incidental asset creation.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nStop on an existing conflicting R ID/path. Load all three and compare their\nmetadata, dependencies, provenance, and ownership to the manifest; verify\nrequired sections and retained GATE-0003/GATE-0005 status.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nCheckpoint B0005 only after every assigned output validates. Keep accepted\noutputs and repair only an incomplete assigned path on resume.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after the three listed files. Do not introduce remote diagnostics, assets, or services.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011 are generated for their allocated IMP records.\n- Each R contract is bounded, traceable, dependency-correct, and has an explicit no-asset assessment.\n- Conflicts halt without overwriting, renumbering, or assigning a replacement ID.\n- The manifest checkpoint follows successful loader and manifest comparison only.\n---\ntask_id: T001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Describe one small, reviewable change\nbrowser_impact: none\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDescribe the smallest complete outcome. State what is in scope and, equally\nimportant, what must not be changed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The intended behaviour is implemented and documented where it affects users or developers.\n- Focused automated tests cover the change and pass.\n- No unrelated refactors, network calls, or credentials are introduced.\n---\ntask_id: F014\nsequence: 14\ntitle: Generate the bounded implementation-runbook authoring collection\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nGenerate only the bootstrap wave of ordinary Supervisor runbooks in\n`projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks/`: a bounded catalogue-expansion\ntask followed by a dispatcher task. The dispatcher allocates at most ten\nauthoring B-series tasks per wave, creates one successor dispatcher, and stops.\nEach authoring task instructs Codex to create only its assigned R-series\nimplementation runbooks under\n`projects/<project-slug>/runbooks/`, then validate their metadata and update the\nmanifest. The successor dispatcher repeats this process until no queued\ncatalogue chapter or unassigned implementation contract remains. Generate an\n`INITIAL.md` context document in `authoring-runbooks/`\nthat points to the canonical `PROJECT_BRIEF.md` and specification.\n\nRegister the generated authoring collection with the source collection by\nwriting `runbooks/.supervisor-children/<project-slug>.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks\"}`. Also\nwrite `authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../runbooks\"}`. These are explicit child-collection\nregistrations; `supervisor-run --run-all` follows them automatically after the\nparent collection is accepted.\n\nEvery dispatcher first expands at most one queued specification/catalogue domain\nchapter (maximum 250 `IMP-*` contracts), validates its coverage, then allocates\nready contracts. If any queued chapter or ready contract remains, it creates no\nmore than ten authoring tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher. If none\nremains, it creates the final audit task instead. This is a durable loop, not a\nrecursive prompt or an unbounded single run.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must use the standard Supervisor front matter\nand contain: precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs; owned\nfiles/data/interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; platform differences;\nverification commands/evidence; and observable acceptance criteria. It must be\nsmall enough for one implementation task, not a vague epic.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must retain machine-readable provenance to the\ncanonical decisions that justify it. Its front matter must declare all of these\nnon-empty fields, using comma-separated values where more than one applies:\n\n```yaml\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#save-state\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-SAVE-001\nauthoring_batch: B0007\nfactory_stages: F003,F005,F012,F013\n```\n\n`source_specifications` points to the smallest relevant canonical\nspecification section; `source_catalogue_ids` identifies the allocated\nimplementation-catalogue records; `authoring_batch` identifies the B-series\nwriter that created the R file; and `factory_stages` identifies the F-series\nstages that established the requirement. This is a traceability trail, not an\ninstruction to inject every F or B runbook into the implementation agent's\nprompt. The R task uses these links to read only the canonical context it needs.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also include a detailed asset assessment.\nIts front matter must always declare both fields below, even when no assets are\nneeded:\n\n```yaml\nasset_impact: required # or not_applicable\nasset_ids: village_gate_main,village_gate_construction # blank only when not_applicable\n```\n\nFor `asset_impact: required`, the B-series writer must reserve stable,\nproduct-specific asset IDs (never generic names such as `image1`), provide an\n`asset_brief` and `visual_style_version`, and include an `## Asset assessment`\nsection explaining the assets' purpose, where they appear, the required visual\nstates/variants, source-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.\nFor `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated\nor source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This\nkeeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product\nasset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway\nthrough coding.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also declare an audio assessment, even\nwhen audio is not needed:\n\n```yaml\naudio_impact: required # or not_applicable\naudio_ids: ember_menu_loop # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_brief: 30-second seamless instrumental menu cue # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_duration_seconds: 30 # 0 only when not_applicable\naudio_loop: required # required, not_required, or not_applicable\naudio_style_version: project-audio-v1\n```\n\nFor `audio_impact: required`, the writer must reserve stable cue IDs, cite the\nrelevant `04-audio-direction.md` section, describe the in-product trigger and\nmix/accessibility expectations, and assign a sensible duration and loop policy.\nThe Supervisor's separate local audio lane then creates a manifest, invokes\nACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For\n`not_applicable`, every audio field has the stated empty/default form so an\notherwise unrelated task cannot silently generate music or sound effects.\n\nEach B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation\nrunbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,\nand leave remaining work for the next bounded batch.\n\nAn unresolved framework, legal, service, design, or other human gate is never\npermission for a B-series writer to omit its assigned R files or wait for an\nearlier B batch to be accepted. The writer produces the bounded contract now,\nrecords the gate and any R-to-R implementation dependency explicitly, and lets\nthe later R-series product-work run pause at that genuine decision. In short:\n**gates block implementation, not runbook authoring**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The initial collection contains only a bounded bootstrap wave; each\n  dispatcher expands at most one 250-contract domain shard, creates at most ten\n  new B-series authoring tasks plus one successor, then exits. It never attempts\n  to materialise the whole game plan.\n- There is exactly one valid B-series authoring runbook per allocated manifest\n  batch, and it creates no more than seven assigned R-series runbooks.\n- B-series runbooks never overwrite an existing R-series contract with a\n  conflicting ID; they stop and report mismatches.\n- Every generated B-series runbook includes its context packet, output list,\n  validation procedure, checkpoint/update procedure, and a clear stop condition.\n- Every generated B-series runbook states that it must author its allocated R\n  files despite unresolved implementation gates or unimplemented R\n  dependencies, retaining those gates in the R contract rather than stopping.\n- Both child-collection registration files exist, contain valid JSON with a\n  relative `runbooks_dir`, and point to the generated authoring and\n  implementation collections respectively.\n- R-series contracts use stable IDs and parse with the Supervisor runbook\n  loader; their declared dependencies match the manifest, every contract has\n  explicit `asset_impact` and `asset_ids` metadata, and asset-required\n  contracts have non-empty stable IDs. Every R contract also has non-empty,\n  valid `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`,\n  and `factory_stages` provenance metadata.\n- Every R-series contract has explicit valid audio metadata. Audio-required\n  contracts have stable IDs, a non-empty cue brief, duration, loop policy,\n  audio-style version, and a source link to the canonical audio direction.\n- The collection contains a final audit B-series task after all authoring\n  batches and catalogue expansions are complete, rather than pretending that\n  thousands of contracts can be reviewed in one generation step.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Structural quality gate for generated B-series and R-series runbooks.\n\nThis validates planning artefacts only; it is never product or release evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nREPOSITORY = ROOT.parents[1]\nMANIFEST_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"\nCATALOGUE_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"\nR_ID, F_ID = re.compile(r\"^R\\d{4}$\"), re.compile(r\"^F\\d{3}$\")\n\ndef values(value):\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else ([value] if value else [])\n\ndef parse_value(value):\n    value = value.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\")\n    if value == \"[]\": return []\n    if value.startswith(\"[\") and value.endswith(\"]\"):\n        return [item.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") for item in value[1:-1].split(\",\") if item.strip()]\n    return value\n\ndef front_matter(path):\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"): return {}\n    end = text.find(\"\\n---\", 4)\n    if end < 0: return {}\n    result, key = {}, None\n    for line in text[4:end].splitlines():\n        if line.lstrip().startswith(\"-\") and key:\n            result.setdefault(key, []).append(parse_value(line.split(\"-\", 1)[1]))\n        elif \":\" in line:\n            key, value = line.split(\":\", 1); key = key.strip(); result[key] = parse_value(value)\n    return result\n\ndef headings(path):\n    return {re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", match.group(1).lower()).strip(\"-\")\n            for match in re.finditer(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*$\", path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"), re.M)}\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--wave\", help=\"validate allocations through this B batch\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    manifest = json.loads(MANIFEST_PATH.read_text())\n    catalogue = json.loads(CATALOGUE_PATH.read_text())\n    batches = {b[\"id\"]: b for b in manifest[\"batches\"]}\n    contracts = manifest[\"r_contracts\"]\n    if args.wave:\n        if args.wave not in batches: parser.error(\"unknown B batch: \" + args.wave)\n        contracts = [c for c in contracts if batches.get(c.get(\"authoring_batch\"), {}).get(\"order\", 999) <= batches[args.wave][\"order\"]]\n    records = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in catalogue[\"contracts\"]}\n    errors, missing, blocked, unverified = [], [], [], []\n    def fail(text): errors.append(text)\n    ids = [c.get(\"id\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    if ids != sorted(ids): fail(\"manifest R IDs are not sequence ordered\")\n    for item, count in Counter(ids).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate manifest R ID \" + item)\n    paths = [c.get(\"output_path\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    for item, count in Counter(paths).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate output path \" + item)\n    assets, browser_paths = {}, defaultdict(list)\n    # The authoring collection is part of the gate: each allocated batch must\n    # exist, identify itself, and be the sole owner of its manifest R IDs.\n    for batch_id, batch_record in batches.items():\n        batch_path = ROOT / \"authoring-runbooks\" / f\"{batch_id}.md\"\n        meta = front_matter(batch_path) if batch_path.is_file() else {}\n        if not meta: fail(f\"{batch_id}: missing or invalid B-series front matter\")\n        elif meta.get(\"task_id\") != batch_id: fail(f\"{batch_id}: task ID mismatch in authoring runbook\")\n        if len(batch_record.get(\"r_contract_ids\", [])) > 7: fail(f\"{batch_id}: exceeds seven-contract batch limit\")\n    for contract in contracts:\n        rid, batch = contract.get(\"id\", \"\"), contract.get(\"authoring_batch\", \"\")\n        if not R_ID.fullmatch(rid): fail(f\"invalid R ID {rid!r}\")\n        if batch not in batches or rid not in batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"r_contract_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: authoring batch ownership mismatch\")\n        catalogue_ids = values(contract.get(\"source_catalogue_ids\"))\n        if not catalogue_ids or contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") not in catalogue_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: missing or inconsistent catalogue provenance\")\n        for cid in catalogue_ids:\n            if cid not in records: fail(f\"{rid}: unknown catalogue ID {cid}\")\n        if contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") in records and not records[contract[\"catalogue_id\"]].get(\"requirement_ids\"): fail(f\"{rid}: catalogue record lacks requirement links\")\n        specs = values(contract.get(\"source_specifications\"))\n        if not specs: fail(f\"{rid}: missing source_specifications\")\n        for link in specs:\n            file_name, _, anchor = link.partition(\"#\"); source = ROOT / file_name\n            if not link.startswith(\"specification/\") or not source.is_file() or (anchor and anchor not in headings(source)):\n                fail(f\"{rid}: unresolved canonical specification link {link}\")\n        stages = values(contract.get(\"factory_stages\"))\n        if not stages or any(not F_ID.fullmatch(s) for s in stages): fail(f\"{rid}: invalid factory_stages\")\n        for dependency in values(contract.get(\"dependencies\")):\n            if dependency not in ids: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} is outside allocation\")\n            elif dependency >= rid: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} does not precede contract\")\n        impact, asset_ids = contract.get(\"asset_impact\"), values(contract.get(\"asset_ids\"))\n        if impact not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}: fail(f\"{rid}: invalid asset_impact\")\n        if \"asset_ids\" not in contract: fail(f\"{rid}: asset_ids absent\")\n        if impact == \"required\":\n            if not asset_ids or not contract.get(\"asset_brief\") or not contract.get(\"visual_style_version\"): fail(f\"{rid}: required assets lack IDs, brief, or style version\")\n            for asset in asset_ids:\n                if not re.fullmatch(r\"ASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\", asset): fail(f\"{rid}: unstable asset ID {asset}\")\n                if asset in assets: fail(f\"asset {asset} ambiguously owned by {assets[asset]} and {rid}\")\n                assets[asset] = rid\n        elif asset_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: non-asset contract reserves asset IDs\")\n        if batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"state\") in {\"blocked_on_gate\", \"blocked\", \"repairable\"}: blocked.append(rid)\n        r_path = REPOSITORY / contract.get(\"output_path\", \"\")\n        if not r_path.is_file(): missing.append(rid); continue\n        meta = front_matter(r_path)\n        for field in (\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if field not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks {field}\")\n        if \"requirement_ids\" not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks requirement_ids\")\n        if meta.get(\"task_id\") != rid: fail(f\"{rid}: task ID mismatch\")\n        if values(meta.get(\"requirement_ids\")) != records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"requirement_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: requirement_ids differ from catalogue\")\n        for field in (\"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if values(meta.get(field)) != values(contract.get(field)): fail(f\"{rid}: {field} differs from manifest\")\n        browser, specs = meta.get(\"browser_impact\", \"not_applicable\"), values(meta.get(\"playwright_spec\", meta.get(\"playwright_specs\")))\n        if browser == \"not_applicable\" and specs: fail(f\"{rid}: browser path on non-browser contract\")\n        if browser != \"not_applicable\" and (not specs or not set(records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"targets\", [])) & {\"web\", \"pwa\"}): fail(f\"{rid}: browser metadata outside browser behaviour scope\")\n        for spec in specs: browser_paths[spec].append(rid)\n        body = r_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if \"## Verification\" not in body: unverified.append(rid)\n        if not re.search(r\"^## Asset assessment\\s*$\", body, re.M | re.I): fail(f\"{rid}: missing explicit Asset assessment section\")\n    for path, owners in browser_paths.items():\n        if len(owners) > 1: fail(f\"duplicate browser test path {path}: {', '.join(owners)}\")\n    graph = {c[\"id\"]: values(c.get(\"dependencies\")) for c in contracts}; active, done = set(), set()\n    def visit(node):\n        if node in active: fail(\"unsupported circular dependency through \" + node); return\n        if node not in done:\n            active.add(node)\n            for dep in graph[node]:\n                if dep in graph: visit(dep)\n            active.remove(node); done.add(node)\n    for node in graph: visit(node)\n    # Discovered families need a canonical source and a category-appropriate\n    # catalogue/verification route. Explicitly held connected scope is a valid\n    # reviewed outcome, not a missing P0 implementation contract.\n    review = ROOT / \"specification/domain-completeness-review.md\"\n    for line in review.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith(\"|\") or line.startswith(\"| System\") or line.startswith(\"| ---\"): continue\n        cells = [cell.strip() for cell in line.split(\"|\")[1:-1]]\n        if len(cells) != 5: continue\n        family, source, _deps, authoring, decision = cells\n        if \"SPEC-\" not in source: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no specification chapter\")\n        if \"hold\" in decision.lower(): continue\n        keywords = [word.lower() for word in re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]{5,}\", family)]\n        searchable = json.dumps(catalogue).lower()\n        if not any(word in searchable for word in keywords): fail(f\"domain family {family}: no catalogue traceability\")\n        if authoring.lower() not in {\"none\", \"n/a\"} and not authoring: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no content/authoring approach\")\n    allocated = {c.get(\"catalogue_id\") for c in contracts}\n    unallocated = [cid for cid in records if cid not in allocated]\n    print(\"Runbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\")\n    chapter_count = len(list((ROOT / \"specification\").glob(\"*.md\")))\n    source_link_count = sum(len(values(c.get(\"source_specifications\"))) for c in contracts)\n    print(f\"canonical specification chapters: {chapter_count}\")\n    print(f\"specification provenance links: {source_link_count}\")\n    for label, result in ((\"catalogue contracts\", list(records)), (\"manifest contracts\", ids), (\"R files missing\", missing), (\"blocked contracts\", blocked), (\"unverified contracts\", unverified), (\"unallocated catalogue contracts\", unallocated), (\"reserved asset IDs\", list(assets)), (\"browser test paths\", list(browser_paths))):\n        print(f\"{label}: {len(result)}\" + (\" (\" + \", \".join(sorted(result)) + \")\" if result else \"\"))\n    for error in errors: print(\"ERROR:\", error)\n    return 1 if errors or missing or unverified else 0\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The allocation ledger and B0005 authoring instructions agree on exactly R0007, R0009, and R0011. I\u2019m preserving the existing manifest state until the three files pass its structural comparison.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0005.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Authoring inputs reviewed; no checkpoint mutation before validation.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"No browser changes are needed for runbook-only contracts.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'test ! -e projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md && test ! -e projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md && test ! -e projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9dfecfd8b0fa3f83584fefc0e2b37cb7248660d3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0007\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Define pure save migration runner\n+dependencies: R0005,R0006\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0007\n+authoring_batch: B0005\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a pure, ordered save-migration runner that accepts an untrusted saved\n+candidate, declares supported predecessor versions, and promotes only a fully\n+validated result. Failed or unsupported candidates retain their original bytes\n+and quarantine disposition; this contract does not select storage or repair\n+player data destructively.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns the versioned content and provenance schema boundary. R0006 owns\n+the local save, validation, current-pointer, known-good retention, and\n+quarantine protocol. Both are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0003 /\n+DEC-0003: a human decision is required for the supported migration window,\n+storage API, quota, and recovery policy before implementation relies on them.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/` migration registry and runner.\n+- `tests/core/save/fixtures/` predecessor, unsupported-version, and failed\n+  candidate fixtures.\n+- Migration registry data and the migration-runner API.\n+\n+The runner owns only pure candidate transformations and their validation\n+boundary. R0006 retains persistence, pointer promotion, and quarantine record\n+ownership; adapters retain any future approved storage mechanism.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Represent every migration as an ordered pure transformation from one declared\n+schema version to its immediate successor. The runner must not read storage,\n+write storage, access a clock, mutate its input, or choose a current save. It\n+returns either one validated candidate with its resulting version or a typed\n+failure that leaves the supplied bytes and source version available to R0006's\n+quarantine path.\n+\n+Before promotion, validate the complete transformed candidate using the save\n+schema, checksum/integrity process, and applicable invariants. Execute each\n+predecessor step once in ascending order; reject cycles, duplicate version\n+steps, gaps, unknown versions, and a result that cannot validate. Do not retry\n+by guessing, drop unknown fields silently, fabricate content, or repair data\n+in place. Only R0006's existing recovery protocol may retain or quarantine the\n+original candidate and promote a validated replacement.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA consume the same shared pure migration API.\n+Their eventual approved local-storage adapters may pass bytes into the runner,\n+but neither target gets a separate migration sequence. PWA cache and update\n+records never enter migration input and cannot be promoted as save data.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not choose a storage driver, support window, retention policy, or recovery\n+policy; do not modify adapters, cache lifecycle, content packages, or current\n+pointers. Do not add export/import, cloud sync, accounts, remote services,\n+network transport, automatic destructive repair, UI, gameplay, product assets,\n+or audio.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The migration runner and synthetic\n+predecessor fixtures need no product asset. Do not create or reserve visual,\n+source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other\n+incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fixtures for every declared predecessor and prove each\n+  takes its ordered path exactly once to a validated candidate.\n+- Prove unsupported versions, duplicate/gapped/cyclic registry definitions,\n+  thrown transformations, checksum failures, and invariant failures leave the\n+  original bytes intact and route to the typed failure/quarantine boundary.\n+- Prove the runner has no storage, network, clock, cache, pointer-promotion,\n+  or mutation dependency; web and PWA adapter fixtures use the same API.\n+- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n+  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n+  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0007 and never renumber or replace it.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain predecessor-chain outputs, input-byte equality assertions for every\n+failure, validation and quarantine-boundary results, purity/static dependency\n+checks, retained GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 evidence, and the successful loader and\n+manifest-comparison record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every declared predecessor version migrates once through ordered pure steps\n+  and only a validated candidate can be returned for promotion.\n+- Unsupported or failed migrations preserve original candidate bytes for the\n+  existing quarantine/recovery protocol and never perform destructive repair.\n+- Migration support-window, storage, and recovery choices remain blocked by\n+  GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no cache, remote, or asset scope is introduced.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4ff79c2636128f903456979de35540c9ad856962\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0009\n+sequence: 9\n+title: Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\n+dependencies: R0002,R0003,R0006\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0012,NFR-0006\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0009\n+authoring_batch: B0005\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; local redacted records only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a bounded, privacy-safe local diagnostic contract for future recovery\n+support: an explicitly consented, redacted local record, clear/delete controls,\n+and a recorder interface with no transport. It must help diagnose a recovery\n+condition without collecting save bytes, dialogue, identity, secrets, or a\n+remote analytics payload.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic\n+fixtures, and R0006 provides local save/recovery and quarantine boundaries.\n+Retain GATE-0005 / DEC-0005: a human decision is required before any transport,\n+retention, hosting, support, or data-handling claim. The gate blocks those\n+implementation choices, not authoring this local boundary.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/diagnostics/` local diagnostic adapter boundary.\n+- `src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*` consent, record, redaction, and\n+  clear-control interface.\n+- `tests/platform/diagnostics.*` deterministic consent, redaction, and local\n+  deletion fixtures.\n+- `docs/privacy-and-recovery.md` diagnostic boundary documentation.\n+- Redacted local diagnostic record and consent-state data schemas.\n+\n+The shared core does not own diagnostic storage or transport. R0006 owns save\n+data and recovery; this task may reference only stable non-content failure\n+categories needed for a local recovery record.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Default diagnostics to absent. The recorder creates a record only after an\n+explicit, revocable local consent state is present; a missing, declined, or\n+withdrawn consent state must create no record. Define a small allow-list such\n+as schema-safe failure category, local timestamp abstraction, app/build\n+identifier placeholder, and recovery action outcome only where the relevant\n+human decisions permit a value. Redact or reject all unrecognised fields.\n+\n+Never capture save snapshots or bytes, checksums, slot names, preferences,\n+dialogue, authored content, free text, input sequences, account data, device\n+identifiers, IP/network data, cookies, tokens, credentials, stack payloads\n+that can expose content, or secrets. Provide a clear-local-record operation\n+that removes only diagnostics after explicit confirmation and visibly reports\n+the local result. The record must not influence save recovery or block play.\n+\n+Enforce a no-network boundary: no provider, endpoint, request client, beacon,\n+upload queue, analytics SDK, background sync, remote retention, or export path\n+is permitted. A future transport proposal is separate work and remains halted\n+at GATE-0005 / DEC-0005.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA share the same consent, redaction, clear, and no-network\n+contract. PWA installation, cache, or offline update state does not grant a\n+diagnostic upload or a separate retention policy. Any target-local storage\n+mechanism remains unselected until the retained gate is resolved.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not integrate analytics, crash reporting, telemetry providers, transport,\n+hosting, remote support, retention schedules, export, identifiers, secrets,\n+accounts, sync, network services, UI screens, save-content inspection,\n+product assets, or audio. Do not claim legal, compliance, or support approval.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. Local redacted records, consent state, and\n+deterministic fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve\n+visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\n+other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fixtures proving no record is created without consent and\n+  that withdrawal prevents subsequent recording.\n+- Test allow-list redaction against save bytes, dialogue/content, slot data,\n+  identifiers, credentials, tokens, request/endpoint fields, stack payloads,\n+  and unknown properties; all must be omitted or rejected.\n+- Test explicit local deletion removes only diagnostic records and leaves the\n+  save/recovery boundary unchanged.\n+- Run a static dependency scan proving no network, transport, provider,\n+  analytics, upload, or background-sync import/configuration exists.\n+- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n+  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n+  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0009 and never renumber or replace it.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain consent-state and absent-record fixture results, redaction/rejection\n+assertions, local-clear results, no-network scan output, the retained\n+GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 record, and the successful loader and manifest-comparison\n+record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Diagnostics are absent without consent, contain only allow-listed redacted\n+  local fields, and can be explicitly deleted without affecting save data.\n+- No diagnostic payload includes save or dialogue data, identity, secrets, or\n+  network/transport fields; no remote diagnostics path is introduced.\n+- Transport, retention, hosting, and support decisions remain blocked by\n+  GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 for both web and PWA paths.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c98007c83426a3f0caa6aed8af7b7bbe4c56c5d2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0011\n+sequence: 11\n+title: Create original-content provenance control\n+dependencies: R0005\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0008,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary,specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0011\n+authoring_batch: B0005\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the original-content provenance control that makes each later authored\n+content package auditable before it enters a build. The control supplies a\n+provenance-record format, source-asset manifest input, validator contract, and\n+human creative-review disposition without creating art, audio, story, or legal\n+approval.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 provides the versioned content package, asset/provenance-manifest schema,\n+and validator boundary. It is the implementation dependency. Human creative\n+review is mandatory for every authored package; legal or licensing review,\n+where applicable, remains under GATE-0007 and cannot be inferred or automated.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `assets/source-manifest.*` provenance input format for later authored\n+  content/assets.\n+- `docs/original-content-review.md` review checklist and recorded disposition.\n+- `tests/content/provenance.*` missing-field and review-state fixtures.\n+- Provenance manifest, review disposition data, and provenance-validator input\n+  contract.\n+\n+R0005 retains content-schema and registry ownership. This task owns only the\n+evidence required to admit later authored material; it does not own assets,\n+licences, gameplay content, or release packaging.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Require a stable content-package reference and a complete provenance record\n+for every later authored content, visual, audio, localisation, map, dialogue,\n+or other expressive entry. The record must identify the entry, its authoring\n+source/type, original-work assertion, any declared permitted source or licence\n+reference when applicable, review status, reviewer identity/role placeholder,\n+review date placeholder, and a human creative-review disposition. Keep the\n+functional reference boundary explicit: a compact party-based turn-adventure\n+scope may inform function only; names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts,\n+UI flows, interaction choreography, and other expression must be original.\n+\n+The validator rejects a missing record, missing required fields, unmatched\n+content reference, invalid disposition, or an entry not marked ready after\n+human creative review. It must not infer originality from an asset filename,\n+automatically clear legal rights, or create substitute content. A reviewer may\n+record a hold or reject disposition; only the human reviewer can record the\n+creative-review outcome. Where a declared source signals licensing or legal\n+review, retain GATE-0007 rather than allowing a technical validator to approve\n+it.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The provenance control is shared content metadata and has no separate web or\n+PWA behaviour. Responsive web and installed PWA consume only content that has\n+passed the same provenance validation; installation, caching, and packaging do\n+not create a provenance exception.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create or select art, audio, dialogue, maps, story, UI, fonts, icons,\n+assets, licences, legal advice, automated legal clearance, release packaging,\n+or target-specific content. Do not treat a reference, filename, or automated\n+check as human creative or legal approval.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This is a control and review contract for\n+future asset-required work; it creates no product asset. Do not create or\n+reserve visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map,\n+or other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run validator fixtures proving missing provenance, required-field omissions,\n+  unmatched IDs, invalid review dispositions, and unreviewed entries are\n+  rejected before content admission.\n+- Run a valid synthetic record fixture with an explicit original-work assertion\n+  and recorded human creative-review disposition; it must be traceable to its\n+  content-package reference.\n+- Review the checklist against the originality boundary and prove that it\n+  retains functional-only reference use and records a hold for any applicable\n+  GATE-0007 legal/licensing concern.\n+- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n+  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n+  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0011 and never renumber or replace it.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain rejected-fixture results, the valid synthetic record and reviewer\n+disposition, the originality-boundary checklist result, any GATE-0007 hold,\n+and the successful loader and manifest-comparison record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Missing or invalid provenance records prevent later authored content from\n+  entering a build; validated records remain traceable to their package entry.\n+- A human creative review disposition is recorded for each authored package;\n+  automated validation does not claim creative, legal, or licensing approval.\n+- The original-expression boundary and any applicable GATE-0007 review remain\n+  explicit, with no asset, audio, or copied expression introduced.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9dfecfd8b0fa3f83584fefc0e2b37cb7248660d3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0007\n+sequence: 7\n+title: Define pure save migration runner\n+dependencies: R0005,R0006\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0007\n+authoring_batch: B0005\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a pure, ordered save-migration runner that accepts an untrusted saved\n+candidate, declares supported predecessor versions, and promotes only a fully\n+validated result. Failed or unsupported candidates retain their original bytes\n+and quarantine disposition; this contract does not select storage or repair\n+player data destructively.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns the versioned content and provenance schema boundary. R0006 owns\n+the local save, validation, current-pointer, known-good retention, and\n+quarantine protocol. Both are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0003 /\n+DEC-0003: a human decision is required for the supported migration window,\n+storage API, quota, and recovery policy before implementation relies on them.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/` migration registry and runner.\n+- `tests/core/save/fixtures/` predecessor, unsupported-version, and failed\n+  candidate fixtures.\n+- Migration registry data and the migration-runner API.\n+\n+The runner owns only pure candidate transformations and their validation\n+boundary. R0006 retains persistence, pointer promotion, and quarantine record\n+ownership; adapters retain any future approved storage mechanism.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Represent every migration as an ordered pure transformation from one declared\n+schema version to its immediate successor. The runner must not read storage,\n+write storage, access a clock, mutate its input, or choose a current save. It\n+returns either one validated candidate with its resulting version or a typed\n+failure that leaves the supplied bytes and source version available to R0006's\n+quarantine path.\n+\n+Before promotion, validate the complete transformed candidate using the save\n+schema, checksum/integrity process, and applicable invariants. Execute each\n+predecessor step once in ascending order; reject cycles, duplicate version\n+steps, gaps, unknown versions, and a result that cannot validate. Do not retry\n+by guessing, drop unknown fields silently, fabricate content, or repair data\n+in place. Only R0006's existing recovery protocol may retain or quarantine the\n+original candidate and promote a validated replacement.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA consume the same shared pure migration API.\n+Their eventual approved local-storage adapters may pass bytes into the runner,\n+but neither target gets a separate migration sequence. PWA cache and update\n+records never enter migration input and cannot be promoted as save data.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not choose a storage driver, support window, retention policy, or recovery\n+policy; do not modify adapters, cache lifecycle, content packages, or current\n+pointers. Do not add export/import, cloud sync, accounts, remote services,\n+network transport, automatic destructive repair, UI, gameplay, product assets,\n+or audio.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The migration runner and synthetic\n+predecessor fixtures need no product asset. Do not create or reserve visual,\n+source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other\n+incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fixtures for every declared predecessor and prove each\n+  takes its ordered path exactly once to a validated candidate.\n+- Prove unsupported versions, duplicate/gapped/cyclic registry definitions,\n+  thrown transformations, checksum failures, and invariant failures leave the\n+  original bytes intact and route to the typed failure/quarantine boundary.\n+- Prove the runner has no storage, network, clock, cache, pointer-promotion,\n+  or mutation dependency; web and PWA adapter fixtures use the same API.\n+- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n+  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n+  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0007 and never renumber or replace it.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain predecessor-chain outputs, input-byte equality assertions for every\n+failure, validation and quarantine-boundary results, purity/static dependency\n+checks, retained GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 evidence, and the successful loader and\n+manifest-comparison record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every declared predecessor version migrates once through ordered pure steps\n+  and only a validated candidate can be returned for promotion.\n+- Unsupported or failed migrations preserve original candidate bytes for the\n+  existing quarantine/recovery protocol and never perform destructive repair.\n+- Migration support-window, storage, and recovery choices remain blocked by\n+  GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no cache, remote, or asset scope is introduced.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4ff79c2636128f903456979de35540c9ad856962\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0009\n+sequence: 9\n+title: Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\n+dependencies: R0002,R0003,R0006\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0012,NFR-0006\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0009\n+authoring_batch: B0005\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; local redacted records only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define a bounded, privacy-safe local diagnostic contract for future recovery\n+support: an explicitly consented, redacted local record, clear/delete controls,\n+and a recorder interface with no transport. It must help diagnose a recovery\n+condition without collecting save bytes, dialogue, identity, secrets, or a\n+remote analytics payload.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic\n+fixtures, and R0006 provides local save/recovery and quarantine boundaries.\n+Retain GATE-0005 / DEC-0005: a human decision is required before any transport,\n+retention, hosting, support, or data-handling claim. The gate blocks those\n+implementation choices, not authoring this local boundary.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/platform/web/diagnostics/` local diagnostic adapter boundary.\n+- `src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*` consent, record, redaction, and\n+  clear-control interface.\n+- `tests/platform/diagnostics.*` deterministic consent, redaction, and local\n+  deletion fixtures.\n+- `docs/privacy-and-recovery.md` diagnostic boundary documentation.\n+- Redacted local diagnostic record and consent-state data schemas.\n+\n+The shared core does not own diagnostic storage or transport. R0006 owns save\n+data and recovery; this task may reference only stable non-content failure\n+categories needed for a local recovery record.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Default diagnostics to absent. The recorder creates a record only after an\n+explicit, revocable local consent state is present; a missing, declined, or\n+withdrawn consent state must create no record. Define a small allow-list such\n+as schema-safe failure category, local timestamp abstraction, app/build\n+identifier placeholder, and recovery action outcome only where the relevant\n+human decisions permit a value. Redact or reject all unrecognised fields.\n+\n+Never capture save snapshots or bytes, checksums, slot names, preferences,\n+dialogue, authored content, free text, input sequences, account data, device\n+identifiers, IP/network data, cookies, tokens, credentials, stack payloads\n+that can expose content, or secrets. Provide a clear-local-record operation\n+that removes only diagnostics after explicit confirmation and visibly reports\n+the local result. The record must not influence save recovery or block play.\n+\n+Enforce a no-network boundary: no provider, endpoint, request client, beacon,\n+upload queue, analytics SDK, background sync, remote retention, or export path\n+is permitted. A future transport proposal is separate work and remains halted\n+at GATE-0005 / DEC-0005.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA share the same consent, redaction, clear, and no-network\n+contract. PWA installation, cache, or offline update state does not grant a\n+diagnostic upload or a separate retention policy. Any target-local storage\n+mechanism remains unselected until the retained gate is resolved.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not integrate analytics, crash reporting, telemetry providers, transport,\n+hosting, remote support, retention schedules, export, identifiers, secrets,\n+accounts, sync, network services, UI screens, save-content inspection,\n+product assets, or audio. Do not claim legal, compliance, or support approval.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. Local redacted records, consent state, and\n+deterministic fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve\n+visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\n+other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fixtures proving no record is created without consent and\n+  that withdrawal prevents subsequent recording.\n+- Test allow-list redaction against save bytes, dialogue/content, slot data,\n+  identifiers, credentials, tokens, request/endpoint fields, stack payloads,\n+  and unknown properties; all must be omitted or rejected.\n+- Test explicit local deletion removes only diagnostic records and leaves the\n+  save/recovery boundary unchanged.\n+- Run a static dependency scan proving no network, transport, provider,\n+  analytics, upload, or background-sync import/configuration exists.\n+- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n+  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n+  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0009 and never renumber or replace it.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain consent-state and absent-record fixture results, redaction/rejection\n+assertions, local-clear results, no-network scan output, the retained\n+GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 record, and the successful loader and manifest-comparison\n+record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Diagnostics are absent without consent, contain only allow-listed redacted\n+  local fields, and can be explicitly deleted without affecting save data.\n+- No diagnostic payload includes save or dialogue data, identity, secrets, or\n+  network/transport fields; no remote diagnostics path is introduced.\n+- Transport, retention, hosting, and support decisions remain blocked by\n+  GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 for both web and PWA paths.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md